sections.interactions:
- **Routing.** hashchange and popstate run route():
  - one section is shown and the others get the hidden attribute;
  - the page scrolls to the top;
  - focus moves to the area's H2 with preventScroll;
  - document.title becomes '{Area} · Settings · {org name}'.
  - The list view focuses the H1 and is titled 'Settings · {org name}'.
- **No hash.** Team when matchMedia('(max-width: 899px)') is false; the list when it is true. A change of that query routes again.
- **'← Settings' on phones.** A real link to settings.html plus the current query. JS pushes the no-hash entry and routes, so the browser's back button returns to the area.
- **Search.** Picking a result first closes the dialog, then navigates, so a result on this page (a hash change) does not leave the dialog open. iconOf() splits hrefs on /[?#]/, so the area results get the Settings icon.
- **?as=** survives every hash change.

sections.content:
**Rows.** A setting row shows a label, its value, a hint and one action:
- Change, for one value;
- Edit, for a person or a channel, which have several fields.

**Editor.** The action opens the row's editor in place, as a <form novalidate> holding:
- the fields;
- the line '[16 px dashed grey loop] Not saved yet', shown only once a value differs;
- Cancel, then Save (violet: a person decides).

**Save.** Nothing changes until Save. Save then:
- validates;
- applies the change to the page's state;
- redraws what depends on it;
- closes the editor and returns focus to the row's action;
- shows a note in the row: '[violet loop] Saved: …' followed by an Undo link.

**Notes and Undo.**
- A note stays 8 s, the Line's duration, and its timer pauses while the pointer or focus is inside it.
- Undo restores the snapshot taken before the save.
- Removing an invitation or a person leaves a placeholder row holding the note, so Undo has a place to put the row back.

**No confirm dialogs and no page-wide save.** For 8 s every change here can be undone, just as a station removed on the Line comes back with Undo.

sections.interactions:
- **Edit email** opens:
  - 'Sender name' (hint 'Clients see it as the sender.');
  - 'Replies go to' (hint 'Where a client’s reply lands.');
  - a fixed line with the Runs on Iqaa badge: 'Every email ends with Runs on Iqaa, once, at the foot. This can’t be changed.'
  - Errors: 'Clients need to see who writes. Write a sender name.' and sign-up's email messages.
  - While the editor is open, the preview follows the typed sender name.
- **Connect** opens a number field:
  - label 'Sufra’s WhatsApp Business number' (or 'Sufra’s number for SMS'), type tel, placeholder '+970 …';
  - hint 'With its country code, starting with +. In this prototype nothing is connected or sent.';
  - buttons Cancel / Connect (violet);
  - error 'Write the number with its country code, starting with +.' The rule: a + followed by 8 to 15 digits, spaces allowed.
- **Once connected**, the row reads 'Connected · +970 … (as typed, in Fragment Mono) · No step sends by WhatsApp yet: choose WhatsApp for a message on the Line.' and offers Disconnect. Note: 'WhatsApp is connected. In this prototype nothing is sent.' with Undo.
- **Disconnect** gives the note 'WhatsApp is disconnected.' with Undo. There is no confirm, because no step uses it.

- **Name, while the editor is open:**
  - the mark panel and 'Where it appears' show the typed name at once;
  - the panel's H3 gets the line '[dashed loop] Preview: not saved yet';
  - the pen writes the initial only when the first letter changes.
- **Name, on Save:**
  - every [data-org-name] and the .ap-org title on this page are renamed;
  - when the initial changed, the pen re-signs the 32 px sidebar mark once;
  - notes: 'Renamed to Lamma. The mark is now an L.' or 'Renamed to Sufra Kitchen. The mark keeps its S.', each with Undo.
  - Names render inside <bdi>.
- **Time zone:** 'now' is recomputed with Intl from the demo instant. Note: 'Time zone set to Africa/Cairo.' with Undo.
- **Hours:** note 'Working hours set to 07:00 to 17:00.' with Undo. In the prototype, other screens keep their own hours.

